---
import Glow from '../components/Glow.astro'
import Frame from '../layouts/Frame.astro'

const repo = 'https://github.com/toni-bobocel/weft'

const chapters = [
  {
    mark: 'Clock',
    lines: ['Order without', 'a master', 'clock.'],
    rows: [
      ['Clock', 'Hybrid logical'],
      ['Tie-break', 'Node id'],
      ['Encoding', 'Fixed-width base 36'],
      ['Drift guard', '60 s, then 4400'],
    ],
    prose:
      '<b>Physical time when machines agree, a counter when they do not.</b> If one edit happened before another, its timestamp is smaller, whatever the wall clocks say. Ids sort as plain strings, so the inspector can show when a write was made, not only its rank.',
  },
  {
    mark: 'Text',
    lines: ['Text that merges', 'letter', 'by letter.'],
    rows: [
      ['Structure', 'RGA sequence'],
      ['Anchor', 'Previous character id'],
      ['Siblings', 'Newest first'],
      ['Deletes', 'Tombstones'],
    ],
    prose:
      '<b>Every character remembers what it was typed after.</b> Because ids follow causality, the integration loop is one comparison, and two words typed at the same spot land whole, side by side. A letter typed into a word someone else deleted keeps its anchor and survives.',
  },
  {
    mark: 'Sync',
    lines: ['Send only', 'what is', 'missing.'],
    rows: [
      ['State', 'Version vector'],
      ['Messages', 'hello, ops'],
      ['Delivery', 'Any order, any count'],
      ['Server', 'Another replica'],
    ],
    prose:
      '<b>Each op carries a gapless number per device.</b> A version vector says exactly what a replica holds, so reconnecting after a week sends the week, not the database. Duplicates are dropped, gaps wait for what they depend on, and the relay is a replica that happens never to edit.',
  },
  {
    mark: 'Proof',
    lines: ['Proven,', 'not', 'argued.'],
    rows: [
      ['Generator', 'fast-check'],
      ['Histories', '1,500 per run, 15,000 in CI'],
      ['Damage', 'Drop, duplicate, reorder, skew'],
      ['Assertion', 'Byte-identical digests'],
    ],
    prose:
      '<b>Convergence is not a claim in a README.</b> A property test writes thousands of histories with concurrent edits, clocks that jump backwards and a network that loses and repeats packets, then requires every replica to hold the same bytes. It found one real bug on its second try.',
  },
]

const records = [
  ['Write the CRDTs instead of adopting Yjs or Automerge', '0001-own-the-crdt.md'],
  ['Hybrid logical clocks for every timestamp', '0002-hybrid-logical-clocks.md'],
  ['RGA for text, tombstones kept', '0003-rga-for-text.md'],
  ['Sync an op log with version vectors; the server is a replica', '0004-op-log-and-version-vectors.md'],
]

const stack = [
  ['TypeScript', 'engine, relay, site'],
  ['No dependencies', 'in the engine'],
  ['node:sqlite', 'relay op log'],
  ['ws', 'relay transport'],
  ['fast-check', 'property tests'],
  ['Vitest', 'test runner'],
  ['three.js', 'this cloud'],
  ['GSAP', 'every motion here'],
]
---

<Frame title="Weft — engine" page="engine">
  <p class="ident">engine<span>how it holds together</span></p>

  <div class="section-mark mono" aria-hidden="true">
    <i><b data-progress></b></i>
    <span data-mark>Clock</span>
  </div>

  <article class="read">
    {
      chapters.map((c) => (
        <section class="chapter" data-chapter={c.mark}>
          <Glow lines={c.lines} />
          <table class="kv mono">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Key</th>
                <th>Value</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {c.rows.map(([k, v]) => (
                <tr>
                  <th>{k}</th>
                  <td>{v}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <p class="prose" set:html={c.prose} />
        </section>
      ))
    }

    <section class="chapter" data-chapter="Records">
      <Glow lines={['Decisions', 'on the', 'record.']} />
      <ul class="records">
        {
          records.map(([title, file]) => (
            <li>
              <a href={`${repo}/blob/main/docs/adr/${file}`}>
                <b>{title}</b>
                <span class="mono dim">↗</span>
              </a>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter" data-chapter="Stack">
      <Glow lines={['Built on', 'very little', 'on purpose.']} />
      <div class="ghosts">
        {
          stack.map(([name, role]) => (
            <div>
              <b>{name}</b>
              <span class="mono dim">{role}</span>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Frame>
